      "problem": "What is the period of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the function takes the form $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx)$ with $B=4.$ \n\nThe horizontal scaling factor is given by \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{B}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the period is\n\n$$\n2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B}=2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can verify this in the graph shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254788/assets/413a0275e89fa3c63161356e7f16f7542b0e38312ebf570980708d648bfbbb8e.png)",
